# Multiline JSDoc for functions (checkJs)

Document **functions, methods, and constructors** with a **multiline** `/** … */` block. Put each `@param`, `@returns`, and description line on its own ` * …` line.

Single-line `/** @param … @returns … */` is for **variables and properties only** (`@type`, `@typedef`, `@import`), not for callable signatures.

## Pattern

```js
/**
 * @param {string} root
 * @returns {Promise<void>}
 */
export async function runSecretSync(root) { ... }

/**
 * @param {string} message
 */
function die(message) { ... }
```

Optional description before tags:

```js
/**
 * Podman secret name = schema key as-is.
 * @param {string} key
 * @returns {string}
 */
export function podmanSecretName(key) { ... }
```

## Do

- One tag per line; align `@param` / `@returns` blocks
- Multiline blocks for arrow functions, `async` callbacks, class methods, and `constructor`
- Keep `@import` / `@typedef` / `@type` on their own single-line comments when they are not function docs

## Don't

```js
// BAD — function docs crammed on one line
/** @param {string} root @returns {Promise<void>} */
export async function runSecretSync(root) { ... }
```

## Arrow callbacks

When typing an inline callback, use a multiline block directly above it:

```js
items.map(
  /**
   * @param {{ key: string }} item
   * @returns {string}
   */
  (item) => item.key,
)
```
